# The web member app is back (2026-08, docs/PRODUCT.md#web-app-status) and, as
# before the teardown, it IS index.html. That is not a stylistic choice — it is
# the only shape Cloudflare Pages supports:
#
#   /*  /index.html  200   real files win; only unmatched paths fall through
#   /*  /app.html    200   308s to /app and loops — every path, site-wide
#   /*  /app         200   swallows real files, including the AASA
#
# Verified against `wrangler pages dev`. A rewrite to /index.html is the one
# destination Pages treats as a fallback rather than an unconditional rewrite;
# any other .html destination is canonicalized to its extensionless form with a
# 308. Changing this line is how the site went down on 2026-08-13.
#
# Member slugs (/patrick) are deliberately NOT listed: they fall through the
# catch-all as a 200 rewrite so the URL survives, which is what lets iOS/macOS
# resolve them against .well-known/apple-app-site-association and open the app
# instead of ever fetching the page. A 301 here would still work on Apple
# devices but would throw away the member context on every other one.
#
# Pages Functions take precedence over this file, so /api/*, /auth/*,
# /calendar/*, /show/:id and the two invite previews are unaffected.

# Member approval was retired in 2026-08 (migration 058); nothing serves these.
/join     /         301
/setup    /members  301
/requests /members  301
/admin    /members  301

# Everything else (member slugs, stale bookmarks, deep links) renders the app
# without changing the URL.
/*  /index.html  200
